# Contributing to MDP
{.lead} Keep the engine pure and keep the look locked — that is the bar for a change.

MDP is small on purpose: a dependency-free engine that compiles one `.mdp` source into design-locked artifacts. Thanks for helping.

---

## Build and run

No install. Plain Node ESM, Node 18 or newer. Clone the repo and run `node packages/core/build.mjs examples/block-compare.mdp`.

That writes `dist/page.html`, `dist/slides.html`, and `dist/flyer.html`. Pass any `.mdp` path to compile a different source. The full set of probes lives in `examples/` (indexed in `examples/README.md`), and fill-in starters in `templates/`.

---

## Project layout

The engine lives in `packages/core/`. Data flows one direction.

```mdp:flow
source -> parse() -> IR { meta, blocks } -> render() -> HTML
```

- `build.mjs` — the CLI: read a source, compile all artifacts, write `dist/`.
- `src/parse.mjs` — source string to the IR.
- `src/inline.mjs` — inline markdown to escaped, safe HTML.
- `src/tokens.mjs` — the locked design system, as CSS.
- `src/render-page.mjs` / `render-slides.mjs` / `render-flyer.mjs` — the artifact solvers.
- `src/stats.mjs` / `compare.mjs` / `callout.mjs` / `flow.mjs` — the shipped blocks.

---

## Adding a new block

A block is a small shared module exporting a `STYLE` string and a `render` function, reused by every renderer so it reads as one designed component. Use `src/compare.mjs` as the model.

1. Create `packages/core/src/<name>.mjs` with a `STYLE` constant and a `render<Name>(block)`. Pass every author string through `inline()` so it is escaped and link schemes are defanged.
2. Use **monochrome tokens only** — `var(--mdp-ink)`, the spacing scale — never literal colors.
3. Use **logical CSS** so the block flips under `dir="rtl"`: `margin-inline-start`, never `left` / `right`.
4. Teach `src/parse.mjs` to emit your typed node; an unknown directive must degrade to readable text.
5. Wire the node into all three renderers and inject your `STYLE`.
6. Update `spec/schema.json` and `SPEC.md` once the shape settles.

---

## Extensions

Core ships a curated block set. Anything beyond it lives in **its own repo** and is discovered the zero-maintenance way: a naming convention plus an npm keyword plus a GitHub topic (the model `eslint-plugin-*` and `slidev-theme-*` use).

Scaffold one in a single command: `npm create mdp-extension my-block` (add `-- --type artifact` for an artifact). Name it `mdp-block-<name>` or `mdp-artifact-<name>`, add the `mdp` / `mdp-block` keywords and a matching GitHub topic, and follow `src/compare.mjs` for the block shape.

:::callout note
`mdp-compiler` has no runtime plugin loader yet, by design. To render a third-party block in a real document you fork or patch core; each generated package's README spells out the exact lines.
:::

---

## Code style

- Plain ESM (`.mjs`). No dependencies, no build step, no bundler.
- **Deterministic.** The render path is pure: no `Date.now()`, no `Math.random()`, no clocks, stable iteration order. Two builds of the same source must be byte-identical. Anything that breaks this is a bug.

---

## Pull requests

Before opening a PR, confirm each of these.

- Every `examples/*.mdp` and `templates/*.mdp` builds and is byte-identical across two runs, and `npm run check:examples` passes. If you add or rename a seed, update its `manifest.json` and run `npm run gen:docs`.
- Output is deterministic: build twice, the HTML is identical.
- The **design lock holds**: no gradients, no shadows, one ink ramp, two weights. A second accent color needs an ADR, not a PR.
- Spec and docs are updated if the format changed.
- If you changed the engine, re-sync the vendored copies: `npm run sync:codex` and `npm run sync:mcp`. CI fails if either is stale.

Keep PRs focused and the diff small. Friendly review, fast merges.
